  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "Sticky: Approval Workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        96,
        -992
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## [YCAT/client-slug] Shorts Approval & Publish\n\n**Per-client copy** of this template. Each client's main-pipeline copy generates magic-link URLs pointing to this client's specific approval webhook path.\n\n### Two trigger modes\n\n**A. Magic-link click** (Webhook GET on `/client-slug-shorts-approve`)\nURL: `N8N_BASE_URL/webhook/client-slug-shorts-approve?clip=<id>&folder=<id>&action=<approve|skip|regenerate>`\n\n**B. Free-text email reply** (Gmail Trigger polls `label:client:client-slug` for replies)\nAgent + Gemini parses the reply → emits per-clip JSON decisions.\n\n### Both paths converge on Switch:\n- approve → Klap export → Gemini gen title+desc+3 hashtags → YouTube upload (CLIENT cred)\n- regenerate → re-trigger main workflow (TODO sticky)\n- skip → log to YCAT sheet\n\n### Per-client setup:\n1. Save As Copy → rename `[YCAT/<Client>] Shorts Approval & Publish`\n2. Search/replace `client-slug` → client slug (affects webhook path + filters)\n3. Wire YCAT Gmail credential to Email Reply trigger\n4. Wire CLIENT YouTube OAuth to YouTube Upload node\n5. Activate.\n\n### Changelog\n- 2026-05-25 (Block 4):\n  - Fixed Klap Export Status URL (back-reference bug)\n  - Fixed Prepare YouTube Upload Payload (back-reference bug)\n  - Forced YouTube `privacyStatus: private` for client-slug self-test\n  - Built regenerate branch (Klap re-submit + Gmail re-review)\n  - Added Log Approve → Sheet after successful upload\n  - Moved Respond to Webhook to fire immediately after magic-link click",
        "height": 668,
        "width": 1320,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
